# spec: magic-cabinet-kitchen-layout

> The spec for Magic Cabinet's kitchen layout engine. Specify at the level where an AI can predict: will this layout fit? Will the installer find it buildable? Will the customer understand it?

---

## 1. IDENTITY

```
name: magic-cabinet-kitchen-layout
purpose: Generate buildable kitchen cabinet layouts from room measurements and customer preferences
scope: IN — measurement input, constraint validation, layout generation, material assignment, installer-facing build sheet. OUT — pricing, ordering, 3D rendering, customer portal
anti-scope: [pricing-engine, order-system, 3d-renderer, customer-auth]
version: 0.1.0
```

---

## 2. WORLD MODEL

### 2.1 Entities

```
entity: Room
  description: A physical kitchen space defined by wall segments
  properties:
    id:
      type: string
      required: true
      constraints: uuid v4
      example: "a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef1234567890"
    name:
      type: string
      required: true
      constraints: 1-100 chars, non-empty
      example: "Main Kitchen"
    wall-count:
      type: number
      required: true
      default: 4
      constraints: 3-8, integer
      example: 4
  states: [draft, measured, validated, locked]
  lifecycle: draft -> measured -> validated -> locked
  cardinality: exactly-one (per project)

entity: Wall
  description: A single wall segment with dimensions and obstacles
  properties:
    id:
      type: string
      required: true
      constraints: uuid v4
      example: "b2c3d4e5-f6a7-8901-bcde-f12345678901"
    length:
      type: number
      required: true
      constraints: >0, <=20000, mm, integer
      example: 3600
    height:
      type: number
      required: true
      constraints: 2000-3500, mm, integer
      example: 2400
    is-load-bearing:
      type: boolean
      required: true
      default: false
      example: false
  states: [blank, has-obstacles, has-cabinets]
  lifecycle: blank -> has-obstacles -> has-cabinets
  cardinality: one-or-many (per room)

entity: Obstacle
  description: Something on a wall that blocks cabinet placement
  properties:
    id:
      type: string
      required: true
      constraints: uuid v4
      example: "c3d4e5f6-a7b8-9012-cdef-123456789012"
    type:
      type: enum[window, door, outlet, pipe, vent, structural, appliance, sink, custom]
      required: true
      example: window
    position-from-left:
      type: number
      required: true
      constraints: >=0, <=wall.length, mm
      example: 800
    width:
      type: number
      required: true
      constraints: >0, <=wall.length, mm
      example: 1200
    height-from-floor:
      type: number
      required: true
      constraints: >=0, <=wall.height, mm
      example: 900
    height:
      type: number
      required: true
      constraints: >0, <=wall.height, mm
      example: 1200
  states: [active, removed]
  lifecycle: active -> removed (no reverse)
  cardinality: zero-or-many (per wall)

entity: Cabinet
  description: A single cabinet placed on a wall
  properties:
    id:
      type: string
      required: true
      constraints: uuid v4
      example: "d4e5f6a7-b8c9-0123-defa-234567890123"
    type:
      type: enum[base, wall, tall, corner, sink-base, appliance-garage, open-shelf, custom]
      required: true
      example: base
    width:
      type: number
      required: true
      constraints: 150, 200, 250, 300, 350, 400, 450, 500, 550, 600, 650, 700, 750, 800, 850, 900, 950, 1000, 1050, 1100, 1150, 1200, mm
      example: 600
    depth:
      type: number
      required: true
      constraints: base/wall/tall -> 600, sink-base -> 650, corner -> 650, all mm
      example: 600
    height:
      type: number
      required: true
      constraints: base -> 720, wall -> 900, tall -> 2100, mm
      example: 720
    material:
      type: entity:Material
      required: true
      example: "white-shaker-oak"
  states: [proposed, confirmed, installed]
  lifecycle: proposed -> confirmed -> installed
  cardinality: zero-or-many (per wall)

entity: Material
  description: A cabinet material/finish combination
  properties:
    id:
      type: string
      required: true
      constraints: kebab-case, unique
      example: "white-shaker-oak"
    name:
      type: string
      required: true
      constraints: 1-100 chars
      example: "White Shaker Oak"
    type:
      type: enum[wood, laminate, thermofoil, acrylic, metal, glass, custom]
      required: true
      example: wood
    cost-per-linear-meter:
      type: number
      required: true
      constraints: >0, USD, 2 decimal places
      example: 285.00
    lead-time-days:
      type: number
      required: true
      constraints: >=0, integer
      example: 14
    in-stock:
      type: boolean
      required: true
      default: true
      example: true
  states: [available, low-stock, backordered, discontinued]
  lifecycle: available -> low-stock -> backordered -> discontinued (backordered -> available possible)
  cardinality: one-or-many
```

### 2.2 Relationships

```
relationship: Room -> Wall
  verb: contains
  cardinality: 1:N
  required: true
  cascade: delete (walls die with room)
  invariants: room.wall-count === count(walls in room)
  example: Room "Main Kitchen" contains Wall "North Wall", Wall "East Wall", Wall "South Wall", Wall "West Wall"

relationship: Wall -> Obstacle
  verb: has
  cardinality: 1:N
  required: false
  cascade: delete
  invariants: obstacle.position-from-left + obstacle.width <= wall.length
  example: Wall "North Wall" has Obstacle "Kitchen Window"

relationship: Wall -> Cabinet
  verb: holds
  cardinality: 1:N
  required: false
  cascade: delete
  invariants: sum(cabinet.width for cabinet on wall) + sum(gap-between-cabinets) <= wall.length - sum(obstacle.width)
  example: Wall "North Wall" holds Cabinet "Sink Base", Cabinet "Corner Lazy Susan"

relationship: Cabinet -> Material
  verb: uses
  cardinality: N:1
  required: true
  cascade: restrict (can't delete material if cabinets use it)
  invariants: none
  example: Cabinet "Sink Base" uses Material "white-shaker-oak"
```

### 2.3 Events

```
event: wall.measured
  trigger: User submits wall dimensions
  payload:
    wall-id: string
    length: number (mm)
    height: number (mm)
  preconditions: [wall.state === blank]
  postconditions: [wall.state === measured, wall.length is set, wall.height is set]
  side-effects: [room.state -> measured if all walls measured]
  probability: null (deterministic)
  frequency: per-wall (once)

event: cabinet.placed
  trigger: Layout engine or manual placement assigns cabinet to wall position
  payload:
    cabinet-id: string
    wall-id: string
    position-from-left: number (mm)
    width: number (mm)
  preconditions:
    - wall.state === has-obstacles
    - position-from-left + width <= wall.length
    - no overlap with any obstacle on wall
    - no overlap with any other cabinet on wall
  postconditions: [cabinet.state === proposed]
  side-effects: [wall.state -> has-cabinets if first cabinet]
  probability: null
  frequency: per-cabinet

event: material.backordered
  trigger: Supplier reports stock depletion
  payload:
    material-id: string
    new-lead-time-days: number
  preconditions: [material.state !== discontinued]
  postconditions: [material.state === backordered, material.in-stock === false, material.lead-time-days === new-lead-time-days]
  side-effects:
    - all cabinet with this material -> flagged for review
    - project timeline extended by new-lead-time-days
  probability: 0.03 (per material per week, based on supplier history)
  frequency: on-demand (triggered externally)

event: layout.validated
  trigger: All constraints pass automated check
  payload:
    room-id: string
  preconditions:
    - all walls in room have length and height
    - all cabinets have material assigned
    - no cabinet-obstacle overlaps
    - all cabinet widths are valid enum values
    - all materials are in-stock or backordered (not discontinued)
  postconditions: [room.state === validated]
  side-effects: none
  probability: null
  frequency: on-demand
```

---

## 3. BEHAVIOR

### 3.1 Capabilities

```
capability: generate-layout
  description: Given a room with measured walls, place cabinets automatically following design rules
  actor: Layout Engine (system)
  inputs:
    room-id: string (required)
    style-preference: enum[modern, traditional, transitional, farmhouse] (required)
    budget-tier: enum[economy, standard, premium] (required)
  outputs:
    walls: Wall[] (with cabinet placements)
    unfilled-gaps: {wall-id: string, gap-mm: number}[] (spaces too small for standard cabinets)
  preconditions:
    - room.state >= measured
    - all walls have length and height
    - at least one material exists per budget-tier
  postconditions:
    - every wall has cabinets placed OR is flagged as unfillable
    - every cabinet has a valid material
    - no obstacles are covered
    - cabinet-to-cabinet gaps <= 50mm
  error-states:
    - room-too-small: room total linear length < 1500mm
    - no-materials: no material matches style + budget
    - impossible-layout: walls have obstacles that prevent any valid cabinet placement
  example:
    input: {room-id: "abc", style: "modern", budget: "standard"}
    output: {walls: [...], unfilled-gaps: [{wall-id: "north", gap-mm: 85}]}
```

### 3.2 Constraints

```
constraint: cabinet-widths-discrete
  type: invariant
  statement: Cabinet widths MUST be from the predefined set [150, 200, 250, ..., 1200] in 50mm increments
  enforcement: strict
  violation-consequence: Layout rejected. No custom widths exist in this system.

constraint: no-obstacle-overlap
  type: invariant
  statement: No cabinet may overlap any obstacle on its wall. Cabinet position + width must not intersect obstacle position + width.
  enforcement: strict
  violation-consequence: Layout rejected. This is physically impossible.

constraint: total-fill
  type: business-rule
  statement: Total cabinet width on a wall MUST <= wall.length. Unfilled space is acceptable but must be reported.
  enforcement: strict
  violation-consequence: Layout rejected. Cabinets can't float beyond the wall.

constraint: material-availability
  type: business-rule
  statement: Cabinets may use available or backordered materials. Discontinued materials are blocked.
  enforcement: strict
  violation-consequence: Cabinet placement blocked until material is reassigned.

constraint: sink-base-position
  type: business-rule
  statement: A sink-base cabinet MUST be placed where a sink obstacle exists on the wall, centered on the obstacle
  enforcement: soft (warn if violated, allow override)
  violation-consequence: Warning shown to designer. Installer will flag during build.
```

---

## 4. UNCERTAINTY

### 4.1 Assumptions

```
assumption: Installers can handle gaps <= 50mm with filler strips
  confidence: high
  basis: Industry standard. All cabinet manufacturers produce filler strips in 25mm increments.
  falsifiable: true
  test: Survey 50 installers: "Can you handle a 50mm gap with standard filler?"
  if-wrong: Maximum allowable gap drops to 25mm. Layout engine must fit cabinets more tightly.

assumption: Users will measure room dimensions within +/- 5mm accuracy
  confidence: medium
  basis: Consumer laser measures are common. No data on our userbase yet.
  falsifiable: true
  test: Compare first 100 submitted measurements to on-site installer verification
  if-wrong: Add 10mm tolerance buffer to all constraints. Or require professional measurement.

assumption: Material lead times from supplier are accurate within +/- 2 days
  confidence: low
  basis: Supplier claims 14-day lead time. No order history to verify.
  falsifiable: true
  test: Track actual delivery dates for first 50 orders
  if-wrong: Add buffer to project timeline. Flag supplier as unreliable. Source backup material.

assumption: Customers understand the difference between base/wall/tall cabinet types
  confidence: speculative
  basis: None. We haven't tested customer comprehension.
  falsifiable: true
  test: Show 10 customers a layout. Ask them to identify base vs wall cabinets.
  if-wrong: Add visual labels to layout view. Remove jargon from customer-facing output.
```

### 4.2 Probabilities

```
outcome-set: installer-revision-rate
  description: Probability that an installer must modify a layout on-site
  branches:
    no-changes: 0.40
    minor-filler-adjustment: 0.35
    cabinet-resized: 0.15
    layout-rejected: 0.10
  basis: Industry benchmark from NKBA 2025 installer survey
  sensitivity: Most affected by measurement accuracy assumption. If measurement error >5mm, layout-rejected doubles.

outcome-set: material-delay-impact
  description: How material backorders affect project completion
  branches:
    on-time: 0.70
    delayed-1-week: 0.15
    delayed-2-weeks: 0.10
    delayed-4-plus-weeks: 0.05
  basis: Supplier SLA data, adjusted for industry trends
  sensitivity: Most affected by in-stock assumption. If in-stock rate drops below 85%, on-time drops to 0.40.

outcome-set: first-layout-acceptance
  description: Will the customer accept the first auto-generated layout?
  branches:
    accept-as-is: 0.25
    accept-with-minor-changes: 0.45
    reject-wants-redesign: 0.20
    reject-switches-to-competitor: 0.10
  basis: Competitor benchmarks (IKEA planner: 55% first-acceptance, ProKitchen: 70%)
  sensitivity: Most affected by style-preference accuracy. If style matching is wrong, reject rate doubles.
```

---

## 5. FAILURE MODES

### 5.1 What breaks?

```
failure: wall-measurement-wrong
  description: Customer submits measurements that are off by >50mm
  cause: Using tape measure instead of laser, measuring to trim instead of drywall, transposing digits
  probability: 0.15 (per project)
  impact: high
  detection: Installer reports discrepancy at site visit. Layout validation doesn't catch this (measurement IS the input).
  recovery: Re-plan layout with corrected measurements. Cabinet order may need revision.
  prevention: Require photo upload of laser measure reading. Add "measure twice" prompt. Offer professional measurement service.

failure: material-discontinued-mid-project
  description: Material becomes discontinued after layout is locked
  cause: Supplier discontinues SKU without notice
  probability: 0.01 (per material per month)
  impact: high
  detection: Weekly supplier catalog sync. Layout engine flags affected cabinets.
  recovery: Suggest nearest-match alternative material. Auto-reassign if customer approves.
  prevention: Prefer materials with >2 year track record. Flag materials <6 months old as "new — risk of discontinuation."

failure: obstacle-missed
  description: Installer finds an obstacle not in the original measurements
  cause: Customer missed an outlet, pipe was behind drywall, appliance dimensions wrong
  probability: 0.20 (per project)
  impact: medium
  detection: Installer reports on site. Must re-plan affected wall.
  recovery: Installer can mark new obstacle in app. Layout engine re-generates for affected wall only.
  prevention: Checklist of common hidden obstacles. Require photo of each wall before layout lock.
```

### 5.2 Edge Cases

```
edge-case: corner-cabinet-on-both-walls
  description: Two corner cabinets placed where walls meet — they conflict for the corner space
  expected-behavior: Corner space is allocated to one cabinet. Second cabinet starts after corner depth.
  current-behavior: unknown
  test: Place corner cabinet on wall A. Place second corner cabinet on adjacent wall B. Verify no overlap.

edge-case: window-height-conflict
  description: Wall cabinet placed where window exists — cabinet bottom is below window top
  expected-behavior: Cabinet blocked. Windows occupy full vertical space from sill to top of wall.
  current-behavior: unknown
  test: Place wall cabinet at position overlapping window. Verify rejection.

edge-case: zero-length-wall
  description: Room has a wall with length 0mm (data entry error or genuinely no wall)
  expected-behavior: Wall rejected at validation. Must have length > 0.
  current-behavior: unknown
  test: Submit room with wall length 0. Verify validation error.

edge-case: all-discontinued-materials
  description: All materials in the system are discontinued. No valid material exists for cabinet assignment.
  expected-behavior: Layout generation fails with clear error. Admin must add materials.
  current-behavior: unknown
  test: Set all materials to discontinued. Try to generate layout. Verify error message.
```

---

## 6. GRANULARITY — the Synecdoche layer

```
nest: Cabinet.door
  entity: Door
    description: A cabinet door/face — what the customer sees
    properties:
      style:
        type: enum[shaker, slab, raised-panel, glass-front, beadboard, louvers, custom]
        required: true
        example: shaker
      hinge-side:
        type: enum[left, right]
        required: true
        constraints: adjacent cabinets should alternate hinge sides when possible
        example: left
      handle-type:
        type: enum[knob, pull, cup, touch-latch, none]
        required: true
        example: pull
      handle-finish:
        type: enum[brushed-nickel, chrome, matte-black, brass, bronze, copper, custom]
        required: true
        example: brushed-nickel
    states: [attached, removed, damaged]
    lifecycle: attached -> removed (removed -> attached possible, attached -> damaged)
    cardinality: one-or-many (per cabinet — tall cabinets can have 2+ doors)

nest: Cabinet.interior
  entity: Interior
    description: What's inside the cabinet
    properties:
      shelf-count:
        type: number
        required: true
        default: 1
        constraints: >=0, <=5, integer
        example: 2
      shelf-adjustable:
        type: boolean
        required: true
        default: true
        example: true
      drawer-count:
        type: number
        required: true
        default: 0
        constraints: >=0, <=4, integer (only for base cabinets)
        example: 0
      soft-close:
        type: boolean
        required: true
        default: false
        example: true
    states: [empty, configured, installed]
    lifecycle: empty -> configured -> installed

nest: Wall.measurement-source
  entity: MeasurementSource
    description: How the wall was measured — affects confidence in dimensions
    properties:
      method:
        type: enum[laser, tape, photo-estimate, professional, unknown]
        required: true
        example: laser
      measured-by:
        type: string
        required: true
        constraints: non-empty
        example: "customer@email.com"
      measured-at:
        type: datetime (ISO 8601)
        required: true
        example: "2026-06-12T14:30:00Z"
      photo-url:
        type: string (URL)
        required: false
        constraints: valid URL, must be an image
        example: null
    states: [submitted, verified, disputed]
    lifecycle: submitted -> verified (submitted -> disputed if installer disagrees)
    cardinality: exactly-one (per wall)

relationship: MeasurementSource -> Wall
  verb: documents
  cardinality: 1:1
  required: true
  cascade: delete
  invariants: none

constraint: measurement-confidence
  type: invariant
  statement: Layout acceptance probability MUST be weighted by measurement method. Laser > tape > photo-estimate > unknown.
  enforcement: soft
  violation-consequence: Layout is still generated but flagged with confidence warning if method is photo-estimate or unknown
```

---

## 7. SIMULATION

### 7.1 Scenarios

```
scenario: first-time-user-measures-kitchen
  description: New user measures their L-shaped kitchen and submits for layout
  initial-state: Room is draft, no walls, no measurements
  steps:
    - User creates Room "My Kitchen" -> room.state = draft
    - User adds Wall "North" with laser-measured length 3600mm -> wall.state = measured, measurement method = laser
    - User adds Wall "East" with laser-measured length 2400mm -> wall.state = measured
    - User adds Obstacle "Sink Window" on North wall at position 800mm, width 1200mm -> wall.state = has-obstacles
    - User adds Obstacle "Range" on East wall at position 600mm, width 900mm -> wall.state = has-obstacles
    - User requests layout generation with style=modern, budget=standard -> layout engine runs
    - Layout engine places cabinets: North wall gets sink-base at 200mm, base cabinets flanking window, corner at east junction. East wall gets base cabinets left of range, tall pantry right of range.
  predicted-outcome: Valid layout with 85% wall coverage. 50mm filler gap on North wall, 100mm filler on East. Total cabinet count: 8-10.
  failure-conditions: Layout rejected due to obstacle placement. Total fill < 60%. Corner conflict.

scenario: material-backorder-during-project
  description: Material goes backordered after layout is locked
  initial-state: Room locked, all cabinets assigned material "white-shaker-oak", project scheduled for 14-day install
  steps:
    - event material.backordered fires for "white-shaker-oak" with new lead time 28 days
    - All cabinets using this material flagged
    - Project timeline extended by 14 days (28 - original 14)
    - Customer notified of delay
    - Option A: customer accepts delay -> project rescheduled
    - Option B: customer switches to "white-shaker-maple" (lead time 7 days) -> material reassigned, project timeline recalculated
  predicted-outcome: 60% of customers accept delay (based on competitor data). 40% switch materials.
  failure-conditions: No alternative material available in same style/price tier. Customer cancels.

scenario: installer-finds-missed-obstacle
  description: Installer arrives on site, discovers a pipe that wasn't in the original measurements
  initial-state: Room locked, all cabinets ordered, installer on site
  steps:
    - Installer discovers 150mm pipe at 2400mm on North wall
    - Installer reports obstacle via app -> new Obstacle created, wall.state = has-obstacles
    - Layout engine re-runs for affected wall only
    - Cabinet at position 2300-2900mm conflicts with pipe at 2400-2550mm
    - Engine removes conflicting cabinet, fills remaining space with smaller cabinets if possible
    - If gap > 300mm after re-plan, installer gets authorization to use filler
  predicted-outcome: 70% resolved same-day with filler. 25% require new cabinet order (1-2 week delay). 5% require full wall re-plan.
  failure-conditions: Multiple missed obstacles on same wall. No valid replacement cabinet widths available.
```

### 7.2 Predictions

```
prediction: First 50 customer layouts will average 2.3 revision cycles before acceptance
  trigger: Product launch
  timeframe: 90 days post-launch
  confidence: 0.65
  measurement: Average revision count per project in database
  actual: pending
  notes: Based on IKEA planner average of 2.8 revisions. We expect slightly better due to constraint engine.

prediction: Material lead time variance will exceed supplier claims by 40%
  trigger: First 50 material orders placed
  timeframe: 180 days post-launch
  confidence: 0.55
  measurement: Compare actual delivery date to quoted lead time
  actual: pending
  notes: Every supplier we've talked to has optimistic lead times. Industry standard is 30-50% variance.

prediction: Obstacle-missed rate will drop from 20% to 8% after photo-upload requirement
  trigger: Photo upload feature released
  timeframe: 90 days after feature launch
  confidence: 0.50
  measurement: Compare installer-reported missed-obstacle rate before vs after feature
  actual: pending
  notes: Assumes users actually upload photos. Adoption rate of photo feature is unknown.
```

